			"date": "2024-06-01T04:04:34.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> on the curly <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.nicknisi.com/@nicknisi\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>nicknisi</span></a></span> question of what you can do to improve the <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/tags/11ty\">#<span>11ty</span></a> ChatGPT experience. There is a big thing you can do and I reckon you are doing it! </p><p>Minimising breaking changes to the API and configuration would go a long way to ensuring based on what little the machine knows is going to continue to be okay advice.</p><p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://changelog.social/@jerod\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>jerod</span></a></span></p>\n<a class=\"p-category\" href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/tags/11ty\">11ty</a>",
